*.log
.DS_Store
# Item: Part 2 secrets-hygiene audit (production-hardening session) --
# .env, .env.backup, and .env.production were the only explicit entries
# before this session; that left any OTHER real .env.* variant (e.g.
# .env.staging, .env.local, .env.testing.local) unignored by name alone.
# A glob + explicit re-allow of .env.example (the one .env* file that
# SHOULD be tracked) is the standard, robust pattern -- covers every past
# and future .env.* variant without needing to enumerate each one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Firebase / service-account credential JSON -- never committed, but no
# prior pattern would have caught one if it were ever added to this repo
# (see KNOWN_RISKS_AND_DECISIONS.md item 8: FCM_CREDENTIALS_PATH is real
# config, just unset/unused today).
*firebase*service*.json
*service-account*.json
